  "description": "Narration compliance battery. Fixed questions across conditions and barrier profiles, scored per (prompt_version, model, adapter_version). Cases are keyed by (condition, patient_id): patient_id alone was unique only within a cohort, which silently scored one condition's personas against another's expected facts. v3 REPLACES `expect_facts` with an AUTHORED `expect` of must/may sets. The old field held retrieval's own top-ranked ids, so recall measured agreement with the retriever rather than relevance — and several entries named barriers the persona does not have (a persona with a car expected to cite \"no reliable way to get to the site\"). Every inherited id was reviewed against the persona and dropped where it was stretched. A must entry that is a LIST is an ALTERNATION: any member grounds the claim, which is how \"B-transport or its origin P-social_determinants.transport\" is graded as the protocol describes it rather than against the author's pick. Recall grades the must-groups; the may-set marks citations that are reasonable without being required. COMPARABILITY: recall figures are NOT comparable to v0.1 or v0.3. Those graded flat sets of four retrieval-derived ids; these grade one to three authored groups. f_recall has its own pre-registered floor for that reason, and a rise over v2 is a change of instrument, not of model.",
